K phosphorylates PLCG2 in p-6Y-SYK:p-Y65,Y76-FCER1G:PLCG2"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Mus musculus", "inferredFrom": [5621363], "species": [{"dbId": 48892, "displayName": "Mus musculus", "name": ["Mus musculus", "M. musculus", "Mm", "house mouse"], "taxId": "10090", "abbreviation": "MMU", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "transition", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}], "reviewed": [{"dbId": 5621625, "displayName": "Geijtenbeek, Teunis B H, 2014-09-02", "dateTime": "2014-09-02 13:22:43", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}], "species": [48887], "summation": [{"dbId": 5621364, "displayName": "Activation of SYK triggers multiple cascades, which induces ...", "text": "Activation of SYK triggers multiple cascades, which induces NF-kB activation through a CARD9-dependent pathway. Phospholipase C-gamma 2 (PLCG2) is one of the key signaling components of the CLEC4E (Mincle)/CLEC6A (Dectin-2) pathway that connects SYK activation to CARD9 recruitment. PLCG2 is activated upon CLEC4E (Mincle)/CLEC6A (Dectin-2) engagement and triggers an intracellular Ca2+ flux. SYK and Src family kinases are upstream of PLCG2. SYK phosphorylates PLCG2 on Y753 and Y759, enhancing the activity of PLCG2 (Gorjestani et al. 2011, Suzuki-Inoue et al. 2004).", "literatureReference": [5607371, 443435], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "isChimeric": false, "category": "transition", "catalystActivity": [{"dbId": 5621361, "displayName": "protein tyrosine kinase activity of pathogens:CLEC6A,CLEC4E:p-Y65,Y76-FCER1G dimer:p-6Y-SYK:PLCG2 [plasma membrane]", "catalyzedEvent": [5621363], "physicalEntity": {"dbId": 5621157, "displayName": "pathogens:CLEC6A,CLEC4E:p-Y65,Y76-FCER1G dimer:p-6Y-SYK:PLCG2 [plasma membran